<title>INDIA: India Corporation Bank cuts prime rate to 13.5 pct.</title>
<headline>India Corporation Bank cuts prime rate to 13.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Corporation Bank is reducing its prime lending rate to 13.5 percent per annum from 14.5 percent, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank's decision is in line with that of some leading Indian banks who have announced cuts in prime lending rate after the Reserve Bank of India cut the bank rate last Wednesday to help boost credit offtake by industry.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
